{
  "_doc": "T-2946: what the jaunts call each building, so a stop's heading, its road notes and the built-so-far walk name it one way: '<name>, <number> Prairie', or '<number> Prairie' where no family is named. Keyed by scene, then by the house's structure id; a coach house, alley or rear building or conservatory takes its house's name ('Marshall Field coach house, 1905 Prairie'). Every name here restates the family its own structure record already names (its name, aka or ticket title); this file adds no claim. A forename is kept only where two houses share a surname, or where the street is known by it. A house whose record gives two families joins them with a hyphen, as the district markers do; one whose identity the record leaves open ('Thorne-associated', 'Identity conflict', 'Cobb-associated') is named by its address alone. tools/jaunt_names.py composes the names; compile_jaunts.py writes them into each compiled jaunt as `places` and refuses a key that is not a structure of its scene.",
